  "ingredients": [
    "24 ounce boneless, skinless chicken thighs",
    "1/4 cup low-carb brown sugar replacement",
    "1/4 cup soy sauce",
    "1/4 cup low-carb ketchup",
    "2 tablespoon apple cider vinegar",
    "1 tablespoon avocado oil",
    "2 teaspoon fresh ginger (grated)",
    "2 teaspoon fresh garlic (minced)",
    "1/2 teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes",
    "400 gram cauliflower rice (frozen)",
    "3 1/2 tablespoon avocado oil",
    "1 teaspoon sesame oil",
    "2 tablespoon soy sauce",
    "3 medium green onion (sliced thin)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Gather and prep all ingredients for the Huli Huli Chicken.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-hawaiian-grilled-huli-huli-chicken/#wprm-recipe-54825-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Keto-Hawaiin-Grilled-Huli-Huli-Chicken-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix together the brown sugar replacement, soy sauce, sugar-free ketchup, vinegar, oil, ginger, garlic, and red pepper flakes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-hawaiian-grilled-huli-huli-chicken/#wprm-recipe-54825-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Keto-Hawaiin-Grilled-Huli-Huli-Chicken-2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add chicken into the marinade and cover with plastic wrap. This can be marinated for a minimum of 2 hours but ideally overnight.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-hawaiian-grilled-huli-huli-chicken/#wprm-recipe-54825-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Keto-Hawaiin-Grilled-Huli-Huli-Chicken-3.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "To prepare the cauliflower rice, add both oils to a pan over medium-high heat. Once hot, add in the spring onion stalks (reserving some of the green parts for garnish) and cook until fragrant, about 1 minute.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-hawaiian-grilled-huli-huli-chicken/#wprm-recipe-54825-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Keto-Hawaiin-Grilled-Huli-Huli-Chicken-4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add in the cauliflower and toss to coat in the oil. Continue to cook for a few minutes until the cauliflower is tender. Add soy sauce and mix into the rice thoroughly. Continue cooking the rice, stirring frequently, until most moisture is out of the rice. Set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-hawaiian-grilled-huli-huli-chicken/#wprm-recipe-54825-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Keto-Hawaiin-Grilled-Huli-Huli-Chicken-5.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prepare the grill to medium heat (350-400F). Once ready, add chicken onto the grill and cook for 8-12 minutes or until cooked through. Baste chicken liberally as it cooks with the leftover marinade.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-hawaiian-grilled-huli-huli-chicken/#wprm-recipe-54825-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Keto-Hawaiin-Grilled-Huli-Huli-Chicken-6.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Re-heat the cauliflower rice if needed and serve with the Huli Huli chicken. Enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-hawaiian-grilled-huli-huli-chicken/#wprm-recipe-54825-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": null
